WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.750 align:start position:0%
 
you can't help but feel resentful  on the 22nd of may 2017 a bombing at the  manchester arena  killed 22 people  salman abadi blew himself up after an  ariana grande concert  in the worst terrorist attack in the uk  since 7-7  i think everybody has a right to take a  sharp intake of breath  and think oh my goodness so much went  wrong  a public inquiry into the bombing has  heard evidence of  unacceptable and unjustified security  failures  this is a forensic look at the missed  opportunities  to stop the manchester bomber  british transport police officer jessica  buller and pcso mark  renshaw are on duty at the city room the  foyer  of the manchester arena at 7 20  the pair leave the city room to take a  meal break they should be no longer  than an hour but they are gone for more  than  two hours at 8 48 two other community  support officers  pcso's brown and maury also take a break  cctv shows them passing salman obadi  in victoria station adjacent to the  arena  he's carrying a heavy rucksack cctv was  picking up a baby  on cameras across the city looking  suspicious you know  with his rooks hours before at 8 51  he enters the city room there are now no  police officers in the foyer  despite instructions from a british  transport police sergeant  that the area should be patrolled at all  times  i think a lot of people just couldn't  hack it and  a lot of me can understand that but he  just feels like a massive failure  what would be the expectation of the  members of the public who  went to that event i think everybody has  a right to expect to be safe and secure  but very clearly there weren't this is  the moment  that a baby is spotted by the site's  security team  security guard mohamed agar sees him  carrying his rucksack  as he crosses the foyer obeidi then  makes his way up this set of stairs  and sits down at the top he stays here  for 20 minutes  out of view it's a cctv black spot  at 9 10 salmon abedi leaves the city  room  carrying his rucksack he returns to the  metro link  where he sits down on the platform for  16 minutes  at 9 29 he makes his way back to the  manchester arena concourse  following the same route while in the  lift  he appears to be adjusting some wiring  below his jacket  at 9 33 he re-enters the venue  and makes his way back to the mezzanine  area which is not covered by cctv  he stays here for just under an hour  at 9 36 pc buller and pcso renshaw  resumed their patrol of the venue  and make their way back to the foyer  more than  two hours after they left for a meal  break  very clearly there were challenges  around  not working or gaps in infrastructure  there were gaps of understanding over  who was responsible for what parts of  the security operation  that existed and there appears to have  been failings by individuals  operating within that security system  it's now  10 15 christopher wilde has been waiting  for his 14 year old daughter  who's at the concert he approaches  muhammad aga  saying he's worried about a suspicious  person with a backpack  mr wilde has already spoken to salman  abadi  who told him he was waiting for someone  the security guard  tells mr wilde he'll report his concerns  as soon as possible  at 10 23 muhammad aga speaks to a  colleague  kyle lawler who's entered the city room  and explains the situation  mr lawler tries to radio in but can't  get through to the control room  to report the suspicious man it's the  you know unwillingness to check it out i  mean  a man alone walking in with a rucksack  to a large packed  you know place it's it's going to raise  alarm bells  it's and yet when they're raised  you know everything's done it's it's  worrying  over the next few minutes mohamed agar  and kyle lawler  have two more conversations about salman  abadi  mr lawler says he had a bad feeling  about him  but there was nothing to really justify  that feeling he also says  he was scared of being wrong and branded  a racist  he attempts to report the situation on  his radio several times  but can't make contact one of the things  that frustrated me across that period in  2017 was we'd seen this rolling wave of  terrorist attacks coming at us from  europe  and we've been putting out a strong  strong message to people like be alert  be aware  you know don't be embarrassed about  reporting things go with your senses  and of course what it appears is that  people heard that message  and they responded and they reported  seeing this guy out of place  in the proximity of the arena and nobody  was responsibility  for dealing with that seem to do  anything at 10  26 he gives up trying and takes up his  position  outside the city room because the show  is ending  at 10 30 concert goers are streaming out  of the arena  salman abadi leaves his hiding place and  walks across the foyer  he is seen on his phone he is smiling  at 10 31 he detonates his bomb  killing 22 people  of the four british transport police  officers on duty at the city room  none are in the foyer they're all in  victoria station  at the time of the blast the main  person we should blame is the bomber  no one in the government really wanted  this to happen no one in the  police ambulance fire none of them  wanted this to happen  they messed up they made human errors  they made massive errors  but the end of the day they didn't pull  the trigger he did  there were missed opportunities  unambiguously  to address  confront approach deal with the  terrorist  what i couldn't be certain of is what  would have been the outcome from doing  that  we just need to learn we need to be  hold those who are accountable  accountable  and we just need to make sure we're  better prepared should it ever happen  again i hope not  i think that is the best revenge any of  us can ever take just carry on  you

